{
  "name": "17 - SETUP - Bookkeeping Data",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Run this once\n\nSelect **Execute workflow** below. It creates three local tables:\n\n- `bookkeeping_profile` — the facts about your books that decide a suggestion: your usual suppliers, the coding rules you already follow, and the amount above which you always want to decide yourself\n- `reconciliation_suggestions` — one row for every transaction the review looked at, what it thinks, and what you decided\n- `reconciliation_runs` — a copy of each review, and what that review cost\n\nNothing leaves your computer. All three start empty.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 420,
        "color": 4
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -660,
        -260
      ],
      "id": "97900000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "name": "Sticky Start Here"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Then what\n\nConnecting Xero is the next step, and it is a one-off. `docs/XERO_RECONCILIATION.md` walks through every click: the Xero developer app first, then the credential in n8n named exactly `Xero (read-only)`.\n\nThe permission screen should say the app wants to **view** your accounting data. If it offers to create, update or delete anything, stop — the Scope field is wrong.",
        "height": 320,
        "width": 420,
        "color": 5
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -200,
        -260
      ],
      "id": "97900000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
      "name": "Sticky Next Step"
    },
